---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="werk" description="werk is a terminal tool for structural dynamics practice. It tracks the gap between what you want and what is true now.">
  <div class="werk-page">

    <div class="werk-hero">
      <div class="werk-glyph">◇</div>
      <h1>werk</h1>
      <p class="werk-subtitle">The Operative Instrument</p>
    </div>

    <div class="werk-body">

      <section class="werk-section">
        <p class="werk-lead">
          A structural dynamics engine for the gap between desire and reality.
        </p>
        <p>
          You want something, and your current situation is different. werk calls that gap a <em>tension</em> and treats it as what moves the work forward.
        </p>
        <p>
          werk computes 13 structural dynamics from the history of the tensions you declare. They are calculated from the actions you record over time.
        </p>
        <p>
          It then passes those dynamics to an AI agent, which works toward the intentions you declared.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="werk-section">
        <h2>How it differs from a task list</h2>
        <p>
          A task list tracks a sequence of steps. werk tracks what you want and what is true now.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each time you update a reality or change a desire, werk keeps the change. Over time that history shows how you approached the work: what changed, when, and what you did about it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Given a declared tension and its context, an agent can propose and carry out actions toward the result you want. You do not have to work out the steps in advance. You have to know what you want and what is true right now.
        </p>
        <p>
          This puts your stated aims in charge of the agent. It gets them from the structure you declared, without fine-tuning or a system prompt.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="werk-section">
        <h2>The Instrument</h2>
        <pre class="werk-terminal"><code>  ◇ Ship a tool that 1000 people use weekly            ○○●●○●● ▸
  ◆ Complete a 50-mile ultramarathon                    ○○○○●●●
  ◇ Be engaged by end of year                           ○○○○○○○
  ◈ Have 48k in liquid savings                          ●○●○●○●
  ◉ Call mom every Sunday                               ●●●●●●●</code></pre>
        <p>
          The terminal interface works by descent: you move deeper into one tension at a time. Pressing space opens the <em>Gaze</em>, which shows the desire and the reality side by side, with the child tensions and the computed dynamics below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="werk-section">
        <h2>13 Structural Dynamics</h2>
        <div class="werk-dynamics-grid">
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Phase</strong><span>Germination → Assimilation → Completion → Momentum</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Tendency</strong><span>Advancing, oscillating, or stagnant</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Magnitude</strong><span>How large the gap between desire and reality</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Conflict</strong><span>When sibling tensions compete for the same life</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Neglect</strong><span>Threads declared important but abandoned</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Oscillation</strong><span>The pattern of advancing then retreating</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Resolution</strong><span>Sustainable forward movement</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Orientation</strong><span>Creative, problem-solving, or reactive</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Compensating strategy</strong><span>The structural lie substituting for progress</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Assimilation</strong><span>Shallow knowing vs embodied change</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Horizon drift</strong><span>Whether deadlines keep moving</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Urgency</strong><span>Temporal pressure from approaching horizons</span></div>
          <div class="werk-dynamic"><strong>Temporal pressure</strong><span>Magnitude × urgency</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="werk-section">
        <h2>The Agent</h2>
        <p>
          Press <code>@</code> on any tension. The agent receives all 13 dynamics, the children and the history, and responds within that scope. It proposes changes such as updating the reality, adding children, resolving the tension or setting a horizon. You accept or reject each one.
        </p>
        <p>
          The agent cannot change anything you have not approved.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="werk-section">
        <h2>The Daimon</h2>
        <p>
          <code>werk watch</code> runs in the background. It stores an observation when a tension is neglected, when two tensions conflict, when oscillation increases or when a horizon passes. The next time you open werk, it tells you how many observations are waiting.
        </p>
        <p>
          It does not send notifications.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="werk-section">
        <h2>The Philosophy</h2>
        <p>
          The name and the vocabulary come from alchemy, where the Great Work meant bringing every part of a life into agreement with the rest. werk is a tool for that kind of work.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is used like an alchemist’s notebook: you record experiments in it, and it shows the patterns in your effort.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="werk-section">
        <h2>Install</h2>
        <pre class="werk-terminal"><code>git clone https://github.com/bierlingm/werk && cargo install --path werk/werk-cli
werk init && werk</code></pre>
        <p class="werk-note">Requires Rust nightly (edition 2024). Built on sd-core: 652 tests, zero unsafe code.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="werk-footer">
        <a href="https://github.com/bierlingm/werk" class="werk-link">GitHub</a>
        <span class="werk-divider">·</span>
        <span class="werk-credit">Built with <a href="https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent">Hermes Agent</a> by <a href="https://nousresearch.com">Nous Research</a></span>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .werk-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .werk-hero {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .werk-glyph {
    font-size: 3rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }

  .werk-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .werk-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .werk-body {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .werk-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .werk-section p + p, .werk-section p + pre, .werk-section pre + p {
    margin-top: 1em;
  }

  .werk-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .werk-lead {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .werk-terminal {
    background: #1a1a1e !important;
    color: #dcdcdc !important;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .werk-terminal code {
    background: none !important;
    color: #dcdcdc !important;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: inherit;
    border: none !important;
  }

  .werk-dynamics-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .werk-dynamic {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .werk-dynamic strong {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    min-width: 180px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .werk-dynamic span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .werk-section code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    background: var(--paper-2);
    padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .werk-note {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .werk-footer {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .werk-footer a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .werk-footer a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .werk-divider {
    margin: 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .werk-link {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .werk-dynamic {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.2rem;
    }
    .werk-dynamic strong {
      min-width: auto;
    }
    .werk-hero h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
